%I A399620 #16 Sep 15 2026 21:44:45
%S A399620 0,0,0,0,2,6,21,40
%N A399620 Minimum number of monochromatic axis-parallel rectangles in a 2-coloring of an n X n grid.
%C A399620 A rectangle is determined by two distinct rows and two distinct columns; its four corners, not necessarily adjacent, must all have the same color.
%e A399620 For n=5, the matrix with rows
%e A399620   00011,
%e A399620   00110,
%e A399620   01001,
%e A399620   11010,
%e A399620   10101
%e A399620 has exactly two monochromatic rectangles. They use rows 1,2 and columns 1,2, and rows 1,3 and columns 1,3. No fewer rectangles is possible, so a(5) = 2.
%e A399620 An 8 X 8 matrix attaining a(8) = 40 has rows
%e A399620   00001111,
%e A399620   00110011,
%e A399620   01011100,
%e A399620   01100101,
%e A399620   10101010,
%e A399620   10110100,
%e A399620   11001001,
%e A399620   11010010.
%Y A399620 Main diagonal of A399621. Cf. A191873, A191965.
%K A399620 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399620 1,5
%A A399620 _Jeremy F. Alm_, Sep 05 2026
